{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Hark when the night is falling
[G]Hear, hear the pipes a' calling
[C]Loudly and [G]proudly calling
[D]Down through the glen
[G]There where the hills are sleeping
[G]Now feel the blood a-leaping
[C]High as the [G]spirits
Of the [D]old Highland [G]men
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Towering in gallant fame
[G]Scotland my mountain hame
[Em]High may your [D]proud standards, [A7]gloriously [D7]wave
[G]Land o' my high endeavour
[G]Land o' the shining rivers
[C]Land o' my [G]heart for ever
[D]Scotland the [G]brave
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]High in the misty Highlands
[G]Oot by the purple islands
[C]Brave are the [G]hearts that beat
[D]Beneath Scottish skies
[G]Wild are the winds tae meet ye
[G]Staunch are the friends that greet ye
[C]Kind as the [G]love that shines
from [D]fair maidens' [G]eyes
{end_of_verse}

